From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:02:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/36] moe cache: the release in-place prefill (TODO #317)
 stands down when a sparse table exists

With any sparse (mmap) table, moe_cache_get_table answers from the tier code, which
refuses a remap published without a freshness round; pf_in_place_locked sets none.
Only reachable with a GTT arena (APU) and mixed tables; inert on discrete GPUs.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
index c91a0a7bc..5f0b25de6 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
@@ -11140,7 +11140,10 @@ bool moe_cache_update_host(const ggml_tensor * weight, const ggml_tensor * weigh
         // and this arm is INERT (never wrong -- the seed and this path are otherwise independent).
         t.remap_n_used  = 0;
         t.remap_prefill = false;
-        if (pf_in_place_locked(t, table, weight_cpy, device, ids, n_used, n_tok, ids_nb0, ids_nb1, stream)) {
+        // With any sparse (mmap) table, moe_cache_get_table answers from our tier, which refuses a remap without a
+        // freshness round (remap_round); this publish sets none, so stand the release's in-place prefill down.
+        if (!g_any_sparse &&
+            pf_in_place_locked(t, table, weight_cpy, device, ids, n_used, n_tok, ids_nb0, ids_nb1, stream)) {
             return true;   // the op reads the arena; no copy of the used residents is made at all
         }
         return false;   // the arena's decode/verify band (and the prefill path when in place declined)
